values ('e1a2b3c4-5d6e-4f81-8a01-1b2c3d4e5f61', 'sensation-and-perception', 'Sensation and Perception', 'Sensation and Perception frames perception as active information processing that transforms physical energy into meaningful experience and action. Students learn how perceptual experience is measured, modeled, and separated from bias, noise, and decision criteria, and how receptors, neurons, circuits, and cortical maps encode sensory information. The course studies vision, audition, body senses, chemical senses, attention, top-down processing, multisensory integration, and constancy; illusions, atypical perception, lifespan change, and culture reveal how perceptual systems work, and students synthesize perception through computational models, applied domains, ethical issues, and a final demonstration or research design.');

